<BaseLayout title="About — Storyfoundry" description="Why Storyfoundry publishes independent fiction on the open web.">
  <section class="page-hero narrow" data-pagefind-body>
    <p class="eyebrow">About Storyfoundry</p>
    <h1>A small home for<br /><em>large imaginings.</em></h1>
  </section>
  <article class="about-prose prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <p class="lead">Storyfoundry is an independent library for fiction published in the open—one chapter, one curious reader, and one impossible world at a time.</p>
    <h2>Why publish this way?</h2>
    <p>The earliest web was full of personal places: odd, handmade rooms where people shared work because they wanted it to exist. This site keeps that spirit while giving long-form stories the care normally reserved for printed books.</p>
    <p>Everything here is comfortable to read on a phone, tablet, or computer. Completed work can be downloaded as EPUB or PDF, so the story does not disappear when you close a browser tab.</p>
    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>There is no algorithm deciding what you should read next. Bookmark the library or subscribe to the RSS feed. New chapters appear when they are ready.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
